Two changes, both only needed under `cargo -Z build-std` (required to
cross-build tier-3 targets like x86_64-unknown-openbsd) -- envmnt builds
fine as-is on a normal stable/prebuilt-std build:

1. Cargo.toml: bump indexmap "^1" -> "^2". Upstream's ^1 pin causes
   IndexMap<K, V, S> arity-defaulting errors (missing the S hasher
   param) against a from-source-built std. indexmap 2.x doesn't hit
   this; envmnt's own usage (IndexMap::new(), type annotations only --
   no removed/renamed APIs) is fully compatible with 2.x as-is.
2. src/lib.rs: drop unused_crate_dependencies from #![deny(...)].
   Building std from source makes the implicit extern crate
   alloc/core/compiler_builtins/panic_abort/panic_unwind/proc_macro
   visible as "unused" under that lint, which envmnt denies as a hard
   error rather than warns.

--- Cargo.toml
+++ Cargo.toml
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 
 [dependencies]
 fsio = "^0.4"
-indexmap = "^1"
+indexmap = "^2"
 
 [dev-dependencies]
 doc-comment = "^0.3"

--- src/lib.rs
+++ src/lib.rs
@@ -120,7 +120,6 @@
     unused_attributes,
     unused_braces,
     unused_comparisons,
-    unused_crate_dependencies,
     unused_doc_comments,
     unused_extern_crates,
     unused_features,
